  "operative_text": "(a_in_person_id) not stated.\n(b_no_id_remedy) not stated.\n(c_mail_ballot_id) not stated.\n(d_proof_of_citizenship) not stated.\n(e_other_rule) not stated.\n(other) Section 1: replaces item (E) of the absentee application contents in 2-6-202(a)(3) with 'The address to mail the ballot outside the county, if applicable;'.\n(other) Section 2: takes effect on becoming law.\n(other) version: Draft 1491001 (2017-02-01): the one-item change; cover lists companion HB 162.\n(other) version: Chaptered 1803427 (2017-04-19): Public Chapter 137 as signed; same operative text as the Draft.\n(other) note: The enacted vehicle for the HB 162 / SB 286 pair. Chaptered text is a scan with garbled characters ('(aX3XE)'); reads as (a)(3)(E). No ID or citizenship content. No amendments saved or listed.\n(note) Off this topic: the bill sets no ID or citizenship-proof rule.",
